The Greek and English Plato editions are adapted from:

  PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit
  commit e37eed2e8a5fed710c3ab0d312249c3fb04d77e0
  data/tlg0059, perseus-grc2 and perseus-eng2 editions
  https://github.com/PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit

Eight Greek files were copied byte-for-byte from:

  jtauber/plato-texts
  commit 3b482c7af8a43444a6e0316f8cb7044a18dbd094
  raw-text/apology.txt, crito.txt, euthyphro.txt, ion.txt, meno.txt,
  phaedo.txt, republic.txt, and symposium.txt
  https://github.com/jtauber/plato-texts

Modifications include TEI-to-text normalization, Stephanus marker indexing,
one enumerated English marker correction, source-bound record extraction,
reviewed commentary and classification, deterministic joins and metrics, and
static HTML generation. Detailed source-by-source provenance is recorded in
raw/plato/SOURCES.md.

The four legacy files under raw/plato/translations/ are quarantined historical
inputs and are not part of the v2.0.0 public distribution.

No audio recording is included in the v2.0.0 knowledge-base release.
